## 2. Web Audio DSP Architecture & Session Persistence ($48\text{ kHz}$ Native)

* **True Audio-Rate Modular Graph:** Built on the native Web Audio API (`AudioContext` at $48\text{ kHz}$ interactive latency), allowing any audio oscillator, noise/weather generator, or CV modulator to connect directly into any audio input or `AudioParam` (frequency, filter cutoff, delay time, wavefolder drive) at full audio sample rate.
* **Sample-Accurate Lookahead Master Clock:** A $30\text{ ms}$ lookahead scheduler inspects `audioContext.currentTime` and schedules multi-bar X0X drum triggers, per-track polyrhythms, pattern chain transitions, Euclidean polyrhythms, sub-bar dividers (`1 / 2 / 4 / 8 BARS`), beat-stepped Chaos/S&H advances, and LFO phase resets $120\text{ ms}$ ahead with catch-up protection.
* **Phase-Lockable LFO Engine (`AudioWorklet` / Phase-Tracked `ConstantSource` + Oscillator Reset):** Supports both ultra-slow free-running frequencies ($0.02\text{–}8.0\text{ Hz}$) and **instant hard phase-reset (`0 rad`)** whenever a trigger arrives at `mod:lfoResetIn` (e.g., from `xox:barTrig` or `xox:trig1`), turning slow sine/triangle waves into tempo-locked rhythmic swells.
* **Zero-Leak One-Shot Node Hygiene:** All percussive drum voices, vactrol sub-pulses, vinyl dust impulses, raindrop pings, and rolling thunder bursts automatically disconnect via `onended` handlers upon envelope completion so long-form ambient/drone sessions run indefinitely without memory or CPU creep.
* **Real-Time Stereo `.wav` Session Recorder (`REC .WAV` / `STOP .WAV`):** Captures the live stereo master bus at native $48\text{ kHz}$ 16-bit PCM and automatically downloads a timestamped `.wav` file on stop.
* **`IndexedDB` Vault & Portable `.json` Patch I/O (`💾` / `📂`):** Saves complete v4 snapshots (all 12 module parameters, 4-voice beat synth settings, all 4 X0X patterns + bar lengths + polyrhythmic lengths, stacked patch cables, modulation matrix slots, and direct output mixer FX states) to `IndexedDB` (`Aether8VaultDB`) while exporting/importing portable `.json` patch files.

